<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Melik Shahnazar II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Melik Shahnazar II was the Armenian melik of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanda">Varanda</a>, one of the five melikdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karabakh">Karabakh</a>, in the mid-eighteenth century. In conflict with the other meliks, he allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panah-ali-khan">Panah Ali Khan</a>, founder of the Karabakh Khanate, and helped him build the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shusha">Shusha</a> in the 1750s, which allowed the khan to bring the Armenian melikdoms under his authority.</p></div>
